    "created_at": "2016-05-05T17:44:05Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-05-05T17:44:05Z",
    "body": "Oh dear, it's complicated. Here is what I've got, for all places in the spec that use \"limited to only non-negative numbers greater than zero\".\n\n| Case | Chrome | Firefox | Edge | Safari |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| [input.size](http://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/?saved=4159) | IndexSizeError | IndexSizeError | Error | IndexSizeError |\n| [colgroup.span](http://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/?saved=4155) | 1 | 1 | Error | 1 |\n| [col.span](http://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/?saved=4156) | 1 | 1 | Error | 1 |\n| [textarea.rows](http://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/?saved=4160) | 2 | IndexSizeError | Error | 2 |\n| [textarea.cols](http://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/?saved=4161) | 20 | IndexSizeError | Error | 20 |\n\nGiven Edge gets away with throwing in all these cases, I think keeping the existing spec would be nice.\n\nBut, if you would prefer, we can introduce a new \"limited to only non-negative numbers greater than zero with default value fallback\" concept that is used for colgroup and col, and maybe for textarea as well.\n\nWDYT @ayg and @cdumez? Two main questions:\n- Should the spec mandate an error for colgroup/col, or fall back to 1? (Only Edge errors currently)\n- Should the spec mandate an error for textarea, or fall back to 2/20? (Edge and Firefox error currently)\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
