    "updated_at": "2016-08-17T11:14:35Z",
    "body": "@smaug----, if you try setting textarea.rows/.cols IDL properties to 0, currently the spec says to throw, which is Edge/Gecko behavior, where Blink/WebKit silently set to the default value instead (which is the behavior if you set rows=0/cols=0 in the markup, and what we already do for col.span and colgroup.span).  Are you okay with changing the spec to the Blink/WebKit behavior?  It seems to be the only way to interop, because Blink/WebKit are not going to want to start throwing and possibly break content.\n\n@annevk I would definitely change col.span and colgroup.span in the spec regardless.  Not only do we have majority agreement, Edge is the only one that implements the current spec, and given their compat hacks, there's no guarantee that's web-compatible.  (I assume they still fall back to old rendering modes for broken sites, right?)\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
